  "details": "I want more badges in the game. But I don't like other peoples suggestions of how to go about it.\n\nCurrently these are the ones available according to the wiki:\n\n-Supporter (get vrc+)\n\n-Early supporter (get vrc+ back in the day)\n\n-VRChat Staff (work at vrchat)*\n\n-VRChat Alumni (get fired from vrchat)*\n\n-VRChat Translator (work on vrchat localization)\n\n-I swear there's another for helping the game alot that I've seen.\n\n-VRChat Wiki Contributor (contribute to the wiki)\n\nIf you look at the current badges available you see a trend. It's helping the game.\n\nI want more badges awarded to those who help the game prosper in some way.\n\nI don't like the idea of just giving badges away for some silly reason. attending an event means nothing, and doesn't help the game. If you get awarded a badge just for attending something, or taking part in something, it creates Fomo for players who start after that time.\n\nI think a badge introduced to the game should be able to be gotten by anyone at any time. assuming they do the good thing that helps the game that would get the badge in the first place.\n\nrough ideas for badges you could introduce:\n\n-Bug bounty badge (Right now people who report massive bugs and exploits get nothing, give them something)\n\n-Years of VRC+ (have it go up each year?)\n\nI'm sure other people can come up with better ideas, But I really wanted to get the point across that I like the idea of badges to reward those who help the game.\n\nThe bug bounty thing is huge though.",
